WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.520
In 1994, French director Luc Besson&nbsp;
unveiled his latest movie: Léon:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.640
The Professional. This action-thriller centers&nbsp;
on the titular hitman, played by Jean Reno,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:15.520
who ends up taking a young girl named Mathilda&nbsp;
under his wing after her family is killed. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.240
actress who played Léon's protégée was none&nbsp;
other than Natalie Portman, and her decision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.880
to join the production at just 11 years old&nbsp;
marked the beginning of her big-screen journey.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.680
Portman's portrayal of Mathilda didn't go&nbsp;
unnoticed, and with each subsequent role she took,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.920
her stock in Hollywood grew dramatically&nbsp;
higher. It was during the 2000s that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.880
really made waves, however, with movies&nbsp;
such as V for Vendetta and Garden State.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:44.800
The next decade kept her busy too, with projects&nbsp;
including Black Swan, Thor, and Annihilation.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.000
These days, Natalie Portman is a household name,&nbsp;
having taken on several career-defining projects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.520
earned numerous awards, and used her platform to&nbsp;
spread awareness on issues near and dear to her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.120
However, thanks to one now-beloved&nbsp;
science-fiction blockbuster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.400
all of this success could very&nbsp;
well have never come to fruition.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.800
1999 was a huge year for Natalie Portman,&nbsp;
seeing as it was the year she joined the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.480
cast of Star Wars: Episode I – The&nbsp;
Phantom Menace. Portman starred as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.760
Padmé Amidala: the queen of Naboo and an&nbsp;
eventual key figure in the Galactic Senate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:21.200
as well as the future wife of Anakin Skywalker&nbsp;
and the mother of their twins, Luke and Leia.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.080
Naturally, landing a job like that should be the&nbsp;
single-greatest career move she could ever make,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.560
right? Well, not exactly — since George&nbsp;
Lucas' second Star Wars trilogy was met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.640
with some seriously harsh reactions from&nbsp;
critics. Not to mention the fact that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.440
fandom fractured with each passing installment,&nbsp;
putting immense pressure on the cast and crew.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:44.400
For Natalie Portman specifically, Revenge of&nbsp;
the Sith came scarily close to ending her run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.960
on the silver screen. She did what she could&nbsp;
with Lucas' notoriously weak dialogue and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.760
tried to give a convincing performance — but&nbsp;
evidently it wasn't enough for most audiences.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.160
By her own admission to New York&nbsp;
Magazine in 2014, she struggled to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.800
acting parts in the wake of her stint in&nbsp;
a galaxy far, far away. Noting that Star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:07.040
Wars led many in the industry to believe&nbsp;
she was a bad actress, Portman recalled:

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:12.080
"I was in the biggest-grossing movie of the&nbsp;
decade, and no director wanted to work with me."

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.560
One likely reason for Natalie Portman losing&nbsp;
Hollywood's good graces post-Star Wars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.720
had to do with the direction of Padmé&nbsp;
Amidala's story. In The Phantom Menace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:25.920
she was introduced as the intelligent, determined&nbsp;
leader of Naboo, who fought back valiantly against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.000
the Separatist invaders. Then, in Attack&nbsp;
of the Clones, she showed that she wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.640
afraid to take the fight to her enemies on&nbsp;
the battlefield of Geonosis, or break every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.440
rule in the book to be with her true love. By the&nbsp;
time Revenge of the Sith rolled around, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.920
much of Padmé's character development&nbsp;
and personality had suddenly disappeared.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.720
As a result of Padmé's reduced role in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.040
Portman didn't have a lot to sink her teeth&nbsp;
into during filming on Revenge of the Sith.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.920
Her work amounted to delivering a few lines&nbsp;
now and again and crying before somehow dying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.560
of sadness — something the film itself did a&nbsp;
poor job of explaining. The movie effectively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.520
relegated Padmé to a plot device designed to&nbsp;
sell moviegoers on Anakin's transformation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.680
into Darth Vader. That's certainly not a&nbsp;
great look for Portman herself, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.480
and things weren't helped along by the fact that&nbsp;
many of her better scenes were cut. In particular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.520
one subplot involving Padmé helping found the&nbsp;
Rebel Alliance wound up on the cutting room floor.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.320
"We are not separatists trying&nbsp;
to leave the Republic. We are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.200
loyalists trying to preserve&nbsp;
democracy in the Republic."

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.760
"I can't believe it has come to this."

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.160
It's plain enough to see that the actress and her&nbsp;
character both got the short end of the stick.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.520
Thankfully, it didn't take too long&nbsp;
for the stigma of Revenge of the Sith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.760
to wear off and for acting gigs to&nbsp;
come Natalie Portman's way once again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:44.480
Her career is still very much intact — and will&nbsp;
hopefully remain as such well into the future.

